ikes - Unfortunately, the creature doesn't have much of the same skills as a common being, even as strong as it is, only being able to swing\ wildly or throw itself on the target to cause some physical damage. </span></p></body>)/Rect[180.873 641.802 519.711 711.812]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj80 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Wobbling Movements - With little technique to use in the self defense context, the cultists can try to evade or run to gain distance of possible agressors. )/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240919204038-03'00')/NM(844ec8dc96c74e098e212ff672c9ebf7)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Wobbling Movements - </span><span style="font-family:Helvetica">With little technique to use in the self defense context, the cultists can try to evad\e or run to gain distance of possible agressors. </span></p></body>)/Rect[180.873 575.41 517.093 621.34]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj81 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Radioactive Suffering - Completely affected by the anomaly, the constant suffering of their bodies, along with their more vulnerable state only allows them to kinda resist against attacks with everything they have, or possibly struggle to keep them away. \)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240919204250-03'00')/NM(0b13cda8c8ee498badf7f34d2c2a2f89)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:2